le-disjoint repository children in parallel worktrees. Each child owns its complete file set, and pedagogish-certain-butterfly is the sole pyproject.toml owner in this epic.\n- Send every repository change through Gerrit.\n- Preserve historical ADR decisions while correcting inaccurate cross references and operational examples.\n- Add no mechanical prose, punctuation, vocabulary, character, or comment enforcement.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Every approved recommendation in the eight child stories is implemented or recorded with its stated evidence.\n- [x] Every child story is closed without force after its own acceptance criteria pass.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each of the seven repository children is merged to main.\n      provenance: environment=rebar.solutions.navateam.com; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Production Gerrit records and origin/main confirmed seven ticket-linked repository commits with status MERGED.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each repository merge has LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n      provenance: environment=rebar.solutions.navateam.com; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Production Gerrit label records for each change showed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submission.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Each repository merge has no unresolved comments at submission.\n      provenance: environment=rebar.solutions.navateam.com; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Production Gerrit detail records showed no unresolved comments at submission for each change.\n- [x] The research child records its conclusion without modifying repository files.\n- [x] The Markdown-only GitHub and Gerrit runbook child skips the full local test suite and passes its focused documentation checks.\n- [x] No child introduces mechanical writing or character enforcement.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685